In summary, the objective function to be minimized, takes the form L(\beta; \mathbf{A}, f, q, \alpha_1, \alpha_2, \lambda) = -\sum_{d=1}^{D-1} \left( \sum_{i=1}^{N} \frac{1}{\sum_{j} h\left(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right)\right)} f_{i,d}g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right) \right) + \lambda \sum_{k=1}^{K} h(\beta_k; \alpha_2). (11) To minimize (11) , we employ the ADAM algorithm [Kingma and Ba, 2014] 8 . The derivative of the objective function is given by \frac{\partial L}{\partial \beta_{k}} = -\sum_{d=1}^{D-1} \sum_{i=1}^{N} f_{i,d} \left( \frac{1}{\sum_{j} h\left(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right)\right)} \frac{\partial g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right)}{\partial \beta_{k}} - g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right) \left( \frac{1}{\sum_{j} h\left(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right)\right)} \right)^{2} \sum_{j=1}^{N} h'(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta)\right)) \frac{\partial g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right)}{\partial \beta_{k}} + \lambda \left(1 - \mathbb{1}_{(k=0)}\right) h'(\beta_{k}), where \frac{\partial g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right)}{\partial \beta_k} = g'\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{k=1}^K A_{i,d,k}\beta_k\right) A_{i,d,k}. (12) Equivalently, written in vector form, this amounts to \frac{\partial L}{\partial \beta} = -\sum_{d=1}^{D-1} \sum_{i=1}^{N} f_{i,d} \frac{1}{\sum_{j} h\left(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right)\right)} \frac{\partial g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right)}{\partial \beta} 
+ \sum_{d=1}^{D-1} \left(\sum_{i=1}^{N} f_{i,d} g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right) \left(\frac{1}{\sum_{j} h\left(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right)\right)}\right)^{2}\right) \left(\sum_{j=1}^{N} h'(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta)\right)) \frac{\partial s_{j,d}(\beta)}{\partial \beta}\right) 
+ \lambda \left[0, h'(\beta_{1}), \dots, h'(\beta_{K})\right]^{T}.

The derivative of the objective function is given by \frac{\partial L}{\partial \beta_{k}} = -\sum_{d=1}^{D-1} \sum_{i=1}^{N} f_{i,d} \left( \frac{1}{\sum_{j} h\left(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right)\right)} \frac{\partial g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right)}{\partial \beta_{k}} - g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right) \left( \frac{1}{\sum_{j} h\left(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right)\right)} \right)^{2} \sum_{j=1}^{N} h'(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta)\right)) \frac{\partial g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right)}{\partial \beta_{k}} + \lambda \left(1 - \mathbb{1}_{(k=0)}\right) h'(\beta_{k}), where \frac{\partial g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right)}{\partial \beta_k} = g'\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{k=1}^K A_{i,d,k}\beta_k\right) A_{i,d,k}. (12) Equivalently, written in vector form, this amounts to \frac{\partial L}{\partial \beta} = -\sum_{d=1}^{D-1} \sum_{i=1}^{N} f_{i,d} \frac{1}{\sum_{j} h\left(g\left(s_{j,d}(\beta; \mathbf{A})\right)\right)} \frac{\partial g\left(s_{i,d}(\beta)\right)}{\partial \beta} 
